The problem states that it takes 6 days to travel by bus and half as many days to travel by car. Half of 6 is 3, so it takes 3 days to travel by car.

Since the trip is to Rochester by bus and back by car, Andrew will travel 6 days by bus plus 3 days by car, for a total of 6 + 3 = 9 days.

\boxed{9}

Johnny started with $20 and added $10, so he had a total of $20 + $10 = $30.

This sum of $30 tripled in value over a year, meaning it multiplied by 3.  So, the amount of money he had after a year is $30 * 3 = $90.

\boxed{90}
